title: $:/plugins/nikorion/base-fields/vocab/status
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki
list: none considering todo doing paused done dropped
radio: yes
blank-value: none
visible-filter: [<currentTiddler>get[role]match[task]] [<currentTiddler>get[role]match[tasklist]] [<currentTiddler>get[role]match[routine]] [<currentTiddler>!has[role]]

Allowed values for the `status` field, in display order.

It is edited with radio buttons (`radio: yes`). `none` stands for an empty field (`blank-value: none`): it is the one checked while the field is empty, and choosing it clears the field. Its label is shown in italics.

Unlike the other vocabularies this one is conditional: `status` says how far along a piece of work is, which only means something on a tiddler that //is// a piece of work. The `visible-filter` field above decides when the control appears — by default, when `role` is `task`, `tasklist` or `routine` (a routine's status is its current run), or when the tiddler has no role at all (every custom field is then offered). When you change these roles, change the sentence of `Fields/status/Stale/Hint` in `language/<lang>/fields.multids` too: it names them for the reader. Widen it there to offer the field on other roles.

To customise the vocabulary, edit the `list` field above (source file: `src/base-fields/vocab/status.tid`), then add the matching entries to `vocab/icons.multids` and to `language/<lang>/vocab.multids`. A value with no translation falls back to its own slug; a value with no icon simply renders without one.
